### Suggested Fix:

To fix the identified issues, add null checks for the `start` and `end` parameters in the `checkStartsWith` and `checkEndsWith` methods, respectively.

```java
public boolean checkStartsWith(String str, String start) {
    if (str == null || start == null) {
        return false;
    }
    return str.regionMatches(!sensitive, 0, start, 0, start.length());
}

public boolean checkEndsWith(String str, String end) {
    if (str == null || end == null) {
        return false;
    }
    final int endLen = end.length();
    return str.regionMatches(!sensitive, str.length() - endLen, end, 0, endLen);
}
```

These changes ensure that the methods handle null values gracefully, preventing NullPointerExceptions and making the code more robust.
